--
N5008 [temp.constr.decl]/1: libstdc++'s _RangeAdaptorClosure declares the
hidden friend `template<typename _Self, typename _Range> requires
derived_from<remove_cvref_t<_Self>, _RangeAdaptorClosure> && ...
operator|(_Range&&, _Self&&)` naming its class unqualified.  The
requires-clause was type-checked in the CALL SITE's scope, the name was not
found, and the candidate was mis-handled downstream ("conversion from 'signed
int [5l]' to 'struct _Partial'" for `arr | views::take(3)`).  The clause is
now checked from the template's own scope.  Non-vacuous: the last assertion
states a wrong value and must FAIL.
